# LINE ENDINGS ARE NORMALISED TO LF IN THE REPOSITORY, ALWAYS.
#
# Without this file, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true can commit CRLF,
# and this fork and its upstream drifted apart exactly that way: `git diff` on
# lib/ask-loop.js reported 1,674 lines changed while `--ignore-cr-at-eol`
# reported none. A merge then produced a 1,675-line conflict in a file whose two
# sides were byte-identical once whitespace was ignored — noise that hides the
# real change and makes every sync a manual review.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text; `eol=lf` fixes what it stores. Working
# copies on Windows still check out however core.autocrlf says — this governs the
# repository, not the desk.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must never touch. A PNG "normalised" as text is a corrupt PNG.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
